  "notes": "USAGE:\n{維持|いじ}する emphasizes keeping something in its existing state over time. It implies ongoing effort to prevent decline or change. The noun form {維持|いじ} is also common, especially in compounds.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {健康|けんこう}を{維持|いじ}する (to maintain health)\n- {秩序|ちつじょ}を{維持|いじ}する (to maintain order)\n- {体重|たいじゅう}を{維持|いじ}する (to maintain one's weight)\n- {維持費|いじひ} (maintenance costs)\n- {現状維持|げんじょういじ} (maintaining the status quo)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {保|たも}つ: to keep, to maintain — native Japanese word with similar meaning, used in everyday speech\n- {保持|ほじ}する: to hold, to retain — emphasizes holding onto something rather than upkeep",
